1. [1mBroken stdout pipe — real divergence.[22m With no reader on stdout, C is killed by [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m (signal 13); the Rust exited 0, because the Rust runtime installs [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m and the translation discarded write errors. Fixed by resetting [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m via a direct [38;5;10mextern "C" fn signal[0m declaration, keeping the crate dependency-free. Covered by [38;5;10mbroken_stdout_pipe_terminates_identically[0m, which borrows a pipe from a helper [38;5;10mcat[0m and kills it rather than racing a short-lived reader.[0m[0m
